+  # rsync's configure AUTO-DETECTS idn2 and ABORTS when the header is
+  # absent — `Failed to find idn2.h for IDN support` — so this was a
+  # dependency on whatever the BUILD MACHINE happened to carry. It built
+  # on x86-64 and aarch64 because those images ship libidn2-dev, and died
+  # on linux/s390x, where nothing does.
+  #
+  # Nothing noticed, because bottle's soname map answers libidn2 with
+  # gnu.org/libidn2 at INSTALL time: `bk undeclared rsync.samba.org`
+  # reports 0 edges, correctly. The map repairs the consequence; the
+  # recipe is what was incomplete.
+  gnu.org/libidn2: '*'
 
